# Caddy — real client IP propagation to loopskill-api (:3370)
# chef_2026-10-09-E. Baseline: 88% of 24h 4xx/5xx were dead-credential MCP 401s
# on /api/mcp/http/ that uvicorn logged as ::1 because neither Caddy nor
# uvicorn propagated the real client IP (Cf-Connecting-IP set by Cloudflare).
#
# WHAT: in every site block / snippet that reverse-proxies to 127.0.0.1:3370
# (the `(loopskill_site)` snippet is the one that matters in production — it
# is imported by both `app.loopskill.io` and the `:3362` tunnel origin), add
# `header_up X-Real-IP {http.request.header.Cf-Connecting-IP}` to the
# reverse_proxy handlers. Caddy 2 already sets X-Forwarded-For itself; the
# X-Real-IP line carries Cloudflare's verified edge-observed client IP so
# uvicorn --proxy-headers (see deploy/loopskill-api.service) rewrites
# request.client to it.
#
# APPLY (prod, via PR merge + ops runbook — do NOT hot-edit):
#   1. Edit /etc/caddy/Caddyfile — inside (loopskill_site), change every
#      `reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3370` to the block form below. A one-time
#      sed is safe because the upstream is uniform on this host:
#        sed -i 's|reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3370$|reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3370 {\n\t\t\theader_up X-Real-IP {http.request.header.Cf-Connecting-IP}\n\t\t}|' /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
#      (Review with `git diff`-style eyeballing + `caddy validate` BEFORE
#      reload; take a timestamped backup first — the house convention.)
#   2. sudo caddy validate --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
#   3. sudo systemctl reload caddy
#   4. Install the unit file from deploy/loopskill-api.service:
#      sudo cp deploy/loopskill-api.service /etc/systemd/system/loopskill-api.service
#      sudo systemctl daemon-reload && sudo systemctl restart loopskill-api
#   5. Verify: `curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' -X POST \
#      -H 'x-api-key: rec_live_doesnotexist' https://app.loopskill.io/api/mcp/http/`
#      → 401; then `journalctl -u loopskill-api -n 3` shows the source as the
#      caller IP (or CF edge), not ::1.
#
# Verification of correctness (why header_up and not a site-wide `header`):
# `header` in a site block mutates the RESPONSE (downstream) direction by
# default; only `header_up` inside reverse_proxy mutates the request as it is
# proxied upstream. A site-wide response-mutating `header` line would have
# silently done nothing — which is exactly the failure mode that let this fix
# sit unlanded for 16 days after being proposed (t_ffdc11c0, 2026-09-24).

(loopskill_api_upstream) {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3370 {
		header_up X-Real-IP {http.request.header.Cf-Connecting-IP}
		flush_interval -1
		transport http {
			read_timeout 0
			response_header_timeout 0
		}
	}
}
